--- inside a standard module, a helper's use of what the program handed is
--- held to its kinds as the program's own calls are, and the refusal names
--- the function the program called: chat's `system` reaches `len` two
--- helpers down (`_chat_with`, then `_body_of`), and an int there is
--- refused naming chat at the program's line. (It had been Magpie's
--- `prior`, until Magpie became a package of its own.)
use llm

m = reach['http://127.0.0.1:1/v1']
talk = ask['hello']
r = chat[m, talk, system = 5]
log[r.ok]
